Another in my long series of suggestions for NH (does anyone on the dev. team
even read this board? Am I wasting my time?)

I think amulets should be a special class of magical items. They should all
be very powerful (either good or bad) like an amulet of life saving, and 
they should be very rare. Furthermore, they should be unpolymorphable (the
way it is now, everyone has 7 or 8 AOLS by the time they reach the endgame),
and they should be identifiable only with a blessed scroll of identify. 
Some suggestions for new, powerful amulets:
Amulet of Magic:
When this amulet is worn, all spellbooks read (including cursed spellbooks)
will be read succesfully. All spells attempted will be casted succesfully,
and all spells will last 4 times longer than they normally would before being
forgotten.

Amulet of Health (supplants amulet vs. poison)
Provides poison resistance intrinsic
Protects from hallucination, sleep, confusion, blindness,  stunning, paralysis
(of all sorts), turning to stone and sickness
triples normal rate of regenration

Amulet of Protection (supplants amulet of reflection)
Provides the following intrinsics:
reflection
displacement
magic protection
fire, cold, shock, disint. resistance
protection from shape changers
protection (like a cloak of protection)

Amulet of Wizard Eye
When this amulet is worn, the wearer can see everything within 10 squares, 
including all physical features of the dungeon (much better than 
clairvoyance) and all monsters (including brainless monsters).

Amulet of Sustenance
When this amulet is worn, the wearer draws sustenance from the amulet, and
has no need for food. This amulet eventually is drained of its sustenance
and crumbles to dust, but it provides the equivalent of 20 or so food rations

And a few bad amulets:
Amulet of Chaotic Magic
Any time you use a scroll, potion or wand it has a totally random effect.
"You zap the wand of death - more -
An area around you is lit

You read the scroll of magic mapping - more -
Your armor turns to dust and falls to the floor"

This should probably include code to make sure that most of the effects
are bad. IE, no wishes, etc.

Amulet of unprotection
When this amulet is worn, all resistances, whether intrinsic or from items,
are nullified. This includes reflection, displacement, magic protection,
cold, fire, sleep, poison, shock, disint. resistance, etc. 

Amulet of cursing
When this amulet is worn, a random item in your backpack is cursed every
20 turns or so

Amulet of ???? (can't think of a clever name)
When this amulet is worn, any monster which attacks you hits you

Amulet of atheism
When this amulet is worn, your alignment becomes atheist. Prayer will cease
to function for you, as will offering. And if you dip this into holy water
to uncurse it, you will get the message "Since you lack faith, your 
efforts are unsuccesful"

Well, that's my idea...

